course: dictionary
lesson: 13263
title: Sound words: glug
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the noise they name. This is called onomatopoeia. Splash, fizz, drip and glug are all sound words, so you can almost hear them.
explain: Glug is an informal word, so you will hear it in chatty talk, on cooking shows and in funny stories more than in formal writing. «She poured a glug of lemonade into her cup.» Here a glug is a quick amount poured out.
explain: Glug can be a noun or a verb. «The bottle glugged as the juice poured out.» Here glugged is an action word. Look at the words around glug to work out which kind it is.
fact: Onomatopoeia means a word that sounds like the noise it names.
fact: «Glug» can mean the gurgling sound liquid makes when it is poured from a bottle.
fact: As a noun, «a glug» can mean a quick amount poured out, as in «a glug of oil».
fact: As a verb, «to glug» means to drink or pour something quickly and noisily.
fact: Glug is informal, so it suits chatty speech, recipes and funny writing more than formal essays.
exercise: «He took a long glug of water from the bottle.» What does glug mean here? | A soft whisper | A thin, dry crack | *An amount of drink swallowed quickly | A loud bang
exercise: Which word in this list is an example of onomatopoeia? | Ancient | Famished | *Glug | Curt
exercise: In «The tap glugged all night», what kind of word is glugged? | A question word | An adjective: a describing word | A noun: a name for a thing | *A verb: an action word
test: «The soup needs a glug of olive oil.» What does a glug of oil mean? | A deep frying pan | A tiny drop that was spilt | A jar that holds oil | *A quick pour of a small amount
test: What kind of word is glug? | A word for a colour | A word from ancient Greek meaning old | *A sound word that copies the noise it names | A word that means very sad
exam: Why is glug called a sound word? | It rhymes with every other word in the dictionary | It means very hungry, like famished | It is only used in maths lessons | *It copies the gurgling noise liquid makes, like onomatopoeia
